target: internal/push/push.go
verify: go test ./internal/push/ -count=1 -run 'TestCheckReadsTheRecordRatherThanBeingTold'
expect: did not reach the decision
why:    Decide's handling of a broken outcome and main's WIRING of it are two different things, and the Python's own history is the reason this is a separate entry: replacing `outcome=run.get("outcome"), unreported=unreported` with None, None passed every suite. That is the same "the channel was never wired" shape that removing --clean-exit left behind, so the table-driven Decide test cannot be what covers it.
--- old
	var outcome string
	if r.Finish != nil {
		outcome = r.Finish.Outcome
	}
--- new
	var outcome string
